Best Walking Shoes for Women of 2026

Comfortable, supportive women's shoes for travel, fitness, work, and all-day wear

October 7th, 2026, updated with 6 months of testing notesHome → Gear Reviews → Footwear

The best walking shoes for women should stay comfortable beyond the first hour. A pair that feels fine grabbing coffee can turn into heel rubbing by hour three of a work shift, or arch fatigue halfway through a travel day spent on airport tile and concrete.

Our testers wore these shoes on daily commutes, errands, travel days, and full shifts on their feet, including two useful tests: seven hours behind a bar on a Saturday night and eight hours into a nursing shift. We tracked performance over a year, from icy sidewalks in January to sun-baked pavement in July, and tested comparable models side by side to see how cushioning and support actually held up against each other rather than just against a spec sheet.

What mattered most was how the shoes felt after hour four rather than minute five: whether the cushioning packed out, whether the fit stayed secure without new hot spots forming, and whether the sole gripped equally well on wet tile and dry sidewalk. We also paid attention to which pairs looked at home on a walk or at a desk, since most people don't want to swap shoes between the two.

Top Pick: The HOKA Bondi SR earns our pick for the best walking shoes for women overall. It held its cushioning through full-day shifts without going flat, gripped equally well on wet tile and dry pavement during testing, carries the American Podiatric Medical Association Seal of Acceptance, and looks unassuming enough to wear from a fitness walk straight into work.

Looking for men’s walking shoes? See our Best Walking Shoes for Men guide for our recommendations

We write mission-driven gear reviews. To find the best gear, we combine expert reviews, everyday user opinions, and rigorous independent trail testing—never native ads or sponsored posts. We are 100% reader-supported and may make a small commission from some qualifying affiliate links. Learn more.

Women’s walking shoes comparison table

The winners

Best overall women’s walking shoes: HOKA Bondi SR

Weight: 23.4 oz (women’s) Drop: 6 mmArch support: NeutralCushioning: MaximumAvailable sizes: 5 - 11 (women’s)What we liked: Cushioned, stable, supportive, comfortable, slip resistant, and can be used for exercise walking or casual wearWhat we didn't like: Bulky; expensive

The HOKA Bondi SR walking shoes are everything we want in a walking shoe: they’re comfortable, cushioned, supportive, durable, slip resistant, and versatile. We can wear these shoes for daily fitness walks, and we can dress them up more casually for work, errands, or casual meet-ups on the town.

Standout features of the Bondi SR include excellent cushion in the midsole for all-day comfort and the slip-resistant tread. These shoes also earned the American Podiatric Medical Association (APMA) Seal of Acceptance, an association that recognizes products beneficial to foot health, which is particularly important for those of us who work on our feet all day.

Learn more in our in-depth review of the HOKA Bondi SR walking shoes.

While the HOKA Bondi SRs work well for active walking and working on your feet all day, they can also be dressed up for casual wear.

The HOKA Bondi SR walking shoes provide lasting comfort on daily walks.

Tester walking on a concrete sidewalk in the HOKA Bondi SR shoes

The HOKA Bondi SR shoes offer excellent slip-resistant traction, making them great for working in slick environments like bars, restaurants, and hospitals.

We tested these shoes on fitness walks, days running errands, and during 7-hour brewery shifts. The slip-resistant tread and balance of cushion and support made them great for long periods on our feet. We also loved how they could blend well as athletic shoes or as a trendy casual look with everyday clothes. As a result, we found ourselves reaching for these shoes the most.

The downside to the HOKA Bondi SR shoes is their bulk. They’re chunky shoes, which may be a style you like, but can also feel cumbersome to others. The weight isn’t a problem for walking, but you wouldn’t want to run in these shoes.

However, if you work on your feet all day, or simply want a walking shoe that is versatile and really comfortable, the HOKA Bondi SR is our top pick.

Best women’s walking shoes for plantar fasciitis: Birkenstock Arizona Soft Footbed Sandals

Weight: 16.2 oz (women’s)Drop: 0 mmArch support: Neutral (forms to your foot)Cushioning: ModerateAvailable sizes: 5 - 12.5 (women’s)What we liked: Cork footbed contours to your foot and offers excellent support and comfort; durable and lasts for many yearsWhat we didn't like: Sandals aren’t ideal for all walking conditions

The Birkenstock Arizona Soft Footbed sandals are our favorite walking shoes for plantar fasciitis because of the foot-contouring cork footbed that comfortably supports your feet. Many Treeline testers have sworn by these shoes for decades, and the author of this guide wore them almost exclusively while dealing with plantar fasciitis.

Learn more in our in-depth review of the Birkenstock Arizona Soft Footbed sandals.

The Birkenstock Arizona Soft Footbed is easy to slip on and offers plenty of comfort and support while walking, making them a great option for injury recovery/prevention. Here the author wears them while recovering from hip replacement surgery.

Birkenstock Arizona Soft Footbed

Walking in the desert in the Birkenstock Arizona Soft Footbed

In addition to the cork midsole, the sandals are durable and can last you many years, making them a great value. The suede upper is comfortable and durable, and the buckles allow you to adjust the shoe to your foot volume. The outsole isn’t the most grippy, but the traction is good enough for most walking surfaces (including non-technical trails).

Not everyone enjoys walking in sandals, though, and these may not work well in particularly wet or cold environments (though we often pair our Arizonas with wool socks when it’s chilly). But if you’re looking for footwear that comfortably supports your feet and will last you many years, the Arizonas are hard to beat.

Best women’s walking shoes with high cushion: On Cloudsurfer 2

